foundation.question_text:
This running-track shape has two straight sides and a semicircle at each end. Calculate its perimeter, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw (0,0) -- (4,0) node[midway,below] {$20\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,2.4) -- (4,2.4) node[midway,above] {$20\text{ m}$};
\draw (4,2.4) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,radius=1.2];
\draw (0,0) arc[start angle=-90,end angle=-270,radius=1.2];
\draw[<->] (-1.9,0) -- (-1.9,2.4) node[midway,left] {$12\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A semicircle sits on top of this rectangle and an identical semicircle is cut out of the bottom. Calculate the perimeter, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,3) node[midway,left] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (2.4,3) node[midway,right] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.4,3) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\draw (0,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,radius=1.2];
\draw[<->] (0,-0.75) -- (2.4,-0.75) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,3) node[midway,left] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (2.4,3) node[midway,right] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw[very thick] (2.4,3) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\draw[very thick] (0,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,radius=1.2];
\node at (1.2,4.5) {$l_1$};
\node at (1.2,1.55) {$l_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Both arcs are semicircles of diameter $8$ cm, and the flat $8$ cm edges are not on the boundary.
$P = 10 + 10 + l_1 + l_2$
$= 20 + 2\times \frac{1}{2}\times \pi(8)$
$= 45.13\text{ cm}$

