\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.5) node[midway,left] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw (3,0) -- (3,1.5) node[midway,right] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw (3,1.5) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.5];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The two curved edges below are semicircles. Calculate the perimeter of the shape in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (4,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2];
\draw (0,0) -- (2,0) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,radius=1];
\draw[dashed] (2,0) -- (4,0);
\fill (3,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (3,0) {$8\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw[very thick] (4,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2];
\draw (0,0) -- (2,0) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw[very thick] (2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,radius=1];
\draw[dashed] (2,0) -- (4,0);
\fill (3,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node at (2,2.35) {$l_1$};
\node at (3,1.35) {$l_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The large arc has diameter $16$ cm and the small arc has diameter $8$ cm; only the left half of the base is straight.
$P = l_1 + l_2 + 8$
$= \frac{1}{2}\times \pi(16) + \frac{1}{2}\times \pi(8) + 8$
$= 12\pi + 8\text{ cm}$

