\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which of these two shapes has the larger perimeter, and by how much? Answer correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.75]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\node[below] at (1.5,0) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\node at (1.5,3.5) {Shape A};
\draw (6,0) -- (9,0) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (6,1.8) -- (9,1.8) node[midway,above] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (9,1.8) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,radius=0.9];
