\draw[<->] (4.6,0) -- (4.6,1.8) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\node at (7.5,3.5) {Shape B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A quarter circle of radius $14$ cm is cut from a square of side $14$ cm. Calculate the exact perimeter of the piece that is left, in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (2.8,0) -- (2.8,2.8) node[midway,right] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.8,2.8) -- (0,2.8) node[midway,above] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.8];
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (2.8,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (0,2.8);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (2.8,0) -- (2.8,2.8) node[midway,right] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.8,2.8) -- (0,2.8) node[midway,above] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\draw[very thick] (2.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.8];
